        - mooted changes to the typologic table
            - added columns
                ?+ add an object column?
                    - name
                        | *phenomenon*
                        | *explanandum*
                    - instances|values
                        | real vs. unreal
                        | fact vs. fiction
                            ?+ synonyms for ‘fiction’
                    / one negative instance|value would be (turning the tables) the rebuttal
                      that the fine tuning is that of life to the cosmos, not the cosmos to life
                ?+ add a column that answers whether an explanation or ‘response’ is wanted?
                    : see e.g. https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/fine-tuning/#DoesFineTuniForLifeRequResp
            ?+ what values of *explanantic ground* for (negative values of) the added columns
                | premise denial
            ?+ what to do with column *name of explanans*?
                | rename simply to *explanans*
                | leave unnamed
                    ∵ already the table claims a payload of explanantia
            ?+ re-describe ‘null, brute fact’ simply as ‘brute fact’
    ─ initial set of possible explanantia and their premises:
        physical necessity
            : privately see `^*• .*${same}$` @ `from the field of fine tuning$` @
              01.logic_tour/._/40.a_search_for_explanations.notes.brec
            : see also `^^multiverse ensemble \+.${same}$`i
            • reality’s structure is explainable by a yet undiscovered theory of fundamental physics ⁠T⁠
            • nothing in ⁠T⁠ itself is unexplained
                / unlike in the present combination (theoretic status quo) of the Standard Model
                  of elementary particle physics and the theory of general relativity
                    : re `status quo` see `^*Friederich.+2026.+Fine-tuning` @ ../sources.brec :
                     ‘Our best current theories of fundamental physics are the Standard Model
                      of elementary particle physics and the theory of general relativity.’ §1.1
                ◦ no contingent parameters (free constants or conditions)
                    / necessary parameters alone, if any
                ◦ no contingent laws
                    / necessary laws alone, if any
                / no dial settings, to borrow the metaphor of fine tuning
                ! necessity is generally too demanding a ground for causal explanation
                    / I expect none of my other explanantia to hold necessarily
                    - what suffices to ground an explanans is that it hang together (cohere) in some
                      satifying way, then we can happily defer investigating its own ultimate cause
                    N.B. yet necessity *is* the characteristic|definitive premise of this explanans
                    order ergo+ the explanantia by Jason Waller’s typologic scheme
                        : re `Jason Waller’s.+scheme` see `${same}` @ ../text.brec
                        - Waller’s scheme incorporates a dichotomy of necessary vs. contingent grounds
                        - meanwhile Friederich’s survey of theoretic physics (‘new physics’) explanantia
                          is ordered (implicitly) by the same dichotomy
                            - the first explanans of the survey grounds on fundamental necessity
                                : see `^*Friederich.+2026.+Fine-tuning` @ ../sources.brec :
                                 ‘first… a so-called *theory of everything* according to which…
                                  the laws and constants of physics… turn out to be dictated
                                  completely by fundamental general principles.’ §2.3
                                - like ⁠T⁠ therefore
                            - the second grounds on a selection mill that processes
                              a [fundamental] grist of contingency
                                : see `^*Friederich.+2026.+Fine-tuning` @ ../sources.brec :
                                 ‘second… a *dynamical* account of the generation of life-friendly
                                  conditions, in analogy to the … “dynamical” evolutionary account
                                  of biological fine-tuning’ §2.3
                        - re the other explanantia:
                            - supernatual design may ground on necessity, as Waller claims
                            - multiverse ensemble and natural design are both selection mills
                              that process a grist of contingency
                                - the former mill is an observer selection effect
                                - the latter mill is a mind that selects from among possible futures
                                  one (technically guides nature) by a principle of practical reason
            • ⁠T⁠ implies the safehold
                / makes it likely or certain to exist, that is
        design
            : privately see `^*• .*${same}$` @ `from the field of fine tuning$` @
              01.logic_tour/._/40.a_search_for_explanations.notes.brec
            : see                 `^^God \+.${same}$`i
            : see `^^multiverse ensemble \+.${same}$`i
        God + design
        multiverse ensemble
            : privately see `^*• .*${same}$` @ `from the field of fine tuning$` @
              01.logic_tour/._/40.a_search_for_explanations.notes.brec
            : see `^^${same} \+.physical necessity$`i
            : see `^^${same} \+.design$`i
    ─ further possible explanantia and their premises:
        multiverse ensemble + physical necessity
            : re `physical necessity` see also
        multiverse ensemble + design



